{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>My God</b> — It is possible that the bet in <b>בך בטחתי</b> ('in you I trusted') stands in place of the vav, like <b>ולמדני</b> in place of the vav, or it is found thus: 'בטחתי בך' — 'I am not worthy that I be ashamed.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The second example (ולמדני) likely alludes to verse 25:5 where the form has a vav; the 'or it is found thus' clause is rendered hyper-literally as the Hebrew is compressed and the syntax of the final inference is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:30.174169642Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}